From 1c77f1f6adece8adb7a669b8e67cde181b665f5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicole@muzz.in>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 03:59:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] web compat: VTTCue.getCueAsHTML, visibilityState, popover,
 MIME, fonts, nosniff

- VTTCue.getCueAsHTML() returns the cue text as a fragment instead of
  being unimplemented (Reddit's video player threw on it).
- document.visibilityState starts visible for documents with a browsing
  context; hidden made sites pause work and lazy-loaders stall.
- [popover] elements that aren't open are display: none.
- extract_mime_type_as_mime re-parses through the mime crate's own type.
- The fontconfig substitute check builds its pattern with
  FcPatternAddString, so names like -apple-system aren't parsed as
  fontconfig syntax and fall back like Chrome.
- local() in @font-face picks the face its style words name; taking the
  family's first face rendered mdBook's sidebar in italics.
- nosniff stylesheets are blocked unless the MIME type is exactly
  text/css (the check used && where the spec needs ||).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
